# Heirloom TEE extension proxy.
#
# Flare's data providers push instructions to whatever URL is recorded on-chain,
# so this hostname has to stay stable across restarts. It is an Azure DNS label
# on a *static* public IP, which is exactly why this works where a quick tunnel
# does not — rotating hostnames are the usual cause of a machine stuck at
# INITIALIZED forever.
#
# Port 6674 is deliberately NOT exposed to the internet. The proxy's HTTP API is
# unauthenticated, so Caddy terminates TLS on 443 and reaches it over loopback,
# and the Azure NSG only ever needs 80/443 open.
sly.southafricanorth.cloudapp.azure.com {
	reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:6674
}
